## Definition of done
- Tests pass ({{TEST_COMMAND}}) and lint is clean. The Stop hook enforces the tests.
- New behaviour has a test; a bug fix starts with a failing test.
- No secrets in code, logs or commits. Refer to environment variable names, never values.
- Diffs stay focused on the task: no drive-by refactors.

## Guardrails in this repo
- `.claude/hooks/guard-bash.mjs` blocks destructive shell commands and asks before risky ones.
- `.claude/hooks/protect-secrets.mjs` keeps `.env` files and keys out of the conversation.
- `.claude/hooks/verify-on-stop.mjs` stops Claude from finishing while tests fail.
- Team rules: `.claude/guard-rules.json` (extra blocked commands) and `.claude/verify.json` (test command, timeout).

## Don't
- Don't push, deploy, or run migrations against shared databases without asking.
- Don't hand-edit generated files, lockfiles or vendored code.
